{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1133514-virtue-vice-for-last-night-from-the-danse-de-la-mort-chronicle-2nd-ed","id":1133514,"title":"Virtue/Vice for \"Last Night\" from the Danse de la Mort Chronicle (2nd Ed.)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-08-24T12:53:03-07:00","id":1133514,"title":"Virtue/Vice for \"Last Night\" from the Danse de la Mort Chronicle (2nd Ed.)","content":"Hoi,<br /> <br /> I am running the <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/1459/Vampire-The-Requiem-Demo-Full?term=danse+de+&amp;test_epoch=0&amp;it=1\" target=\"_blank\">Danse de la Mort Chronicle</a> using the 2nd Edition rules and as I am preparing for the &quot;Last Night&quot; Story, I am not sure what Virtue/Vice combo to assign to the protagonists. What do you think are the appropriate Virtue/Vice combos for the main characters?<br /> <br /> On a side note, that chronicle is absolutely fantastic. Even though it requires a lot of tinkering to run using the 2nd Edition rules, I can't recommend it enough. Matthew McFarland is now one of my favorite authors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14844-chubby-russian","name":"Chubby Russian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14844_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T13:15:32-07:00","id":1133526,"title":"","content":"Assuming you'll ST it; why aren't the players picking their virtue/vice? Or Masque/Dirge in any case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T13:29:08-07:00","id":1133530,"title":"","content":"Malus,<br /> <br /> Valid point. However, Danse de la Mort is an introductory chronicle that comes with pre-generated characters. I am simply updating the characters for the 2nd Edition.<br /> <br /> I can understand letting the players pick/change the Mask/Dirge for the characters, since they are playing as Kindred for 7/8 Stories in the Chronicle. However, Last Night is just one Story. It is also pretty short - it will likely last no more than one Chapter. So I don't think my players really want to spend time figuring out the Virtue/Vice for just one session. They already want to hand-waive a whole bunch of &quot;mortal&quot; rules for Last Night, like Integrity.<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> Also because they can't be trusted with decision-making power! This is not a democracy! Just kidding, lol.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":14844,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14844-chubby-russian","user":"Chubby Russian","date":". 08-24-2017, 04:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14844-chubby-russian","name":"Chubby Russian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14844_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T13:43:55-07:00","id":1133535,"title":"","content":"Since the PCs are super fresh, I would do something slightly different: The characters get a Mask to replace their Virtue as normal. This Mask is directly based on their lost human lives. However, they still have their human Vice until the end of the first Story. At which point you may as well let the players decide. You could allow them to delay this switch for a bit longer too.<br /> <br /> This could also be a nice bit of bringing in the psychological change via the character sheet. They are not quite proper vampires yet, which feeds well into 2e's theme of slowly growing into being a proper vampire, instead of it being a instant binary switch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T13:49:51-07:00","id":1133537,"title":"","content":"Saibot,<br /> <br /> Great idea, but two things ruin it in this particular instance:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">1) The mortal Story is not actually the first Story in the Chronicle. The first Story (&quot;Mary's Child&quot;) is the newly-Embraced Kindred (PCs) waking up in a park with no recollection of the events that led to their Embrace. The second Story is &quot;Last Night&quot; - the prelude where the PCs re-live the events of their last night as mortals.<br /> </div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">2) My group has already finished Mary's Child, so they already started with Mask, Dirge and all the other bells and whistles of the vampire condition.</div> <br /> Thank you for the nice idea though. I will probably steal it to use another night.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14844-chubby-russian","name":"Chubby Russian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14844_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T14:12:34-07:00","id":1133546,"title":"","content":"Oh, I misunderstood the request. In that case the simple solution is just taking the old Vice/Virtue and turning them into their adjective forms. It is only for one story so I do not think that is too much of a problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-29T08:09:18-07:00","id":1135158,"title":"","content":"Hi Chubby Russian, why not just use the originally assigned Virtue/Vice from the 1e demo? Are you not using the set characters from the demo?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1161-gravitas-man","name":"Gravitas Man","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1161_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-29T09:39:51-07:00","id":1135185,"title":"","content":"Gravitas Man,<br /> <br /> Well, my group is using the original characters. However, there is a couple of reasons I don't feel like using the original Virtue/Vice combos:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">1) The Virtue/Vice mechanics changed between editions. The characters in the 2nd Ed. are supposed to be able to regain WP through the Vice more frequently and easier than in the 1st Ed. The original Vices don't really support that well, at least in my mind;</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">2) The Virtue/Vice feel changed between the editions. I believe they are supposed to be much more &quot;mundane&quot; and less &quot;pretentious,&quot; if you will. It is not <b>the Vice of Greed</b>, but <b>your character is cheap</b> - does that make sense? It looks like they should be much more down-to-earth; and</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">3) In the 2nd Ed. Virtues and Vices have to be adjectives, if I remember correctly. Adjectives based on some of the original Virtues/Vices sound terrible, lol.</div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":14844,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14844-chubby-russian","user":"Chubby Russian","date":". 08-29-2017, 12:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14844-chubby-russian","name":"Chubby Russian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14844_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-29T12:05:46-07:00","id":1135230,"title":"","content":"Being cheap (stingy) doesn't HAVE to be a symptom of Greed. It could stem from Envy. (I don't want anyone having more than I do.) Pride. (I have more money because I'm better than you and this proves it.) Lust. (Money is the only thing worth having.) Gluttony (There is no such thing as having too much money.) Wrath (I earned my money. Fuck anyone who tries to take it.) Sloth. (I don't care enough about you or your problems to trouble myself to give you money.) <br /> The point sort of was the fact that you can put any number of self aggrandizing behavior that victimized others under multiple sins which is also why getting willpower back under a key Vice was easier than a Virtue refill.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-29T12:29:55-07:00","id":1135244,"title":"","content":"Most of the 1e virtues and vices have direct equivalents in the example virtues and vices in GMC, and those that don't could be substituted for indirect equivalents or custom ones made for them.<br /> <br /> Charity = Generous<br /> Hope = Hopeful<br /> Justice = Just or Righteous<br /> Prudence = Patient<br /> <br /> Greed = Greedy<br /> Pride = Arrogant or Ambitious<br /> Sloth = Pessimistic<br /> Wrath = Violent or Hateful<br /> <br /> That leaves Faith, Fortitude, Temperance, Envy, Gluttony, and Lust.<br /> <br /> Faith could easily become Faithful, which could restore Willpower when the character puts herself at risk in defense of her beliefs. Fortitude could become Resolute, which could restore Willpower when the character sticks to a chosen course of action despite great adversity. Temperance could become Moderate, which could restore Willpower when the character turns down an opportunity to gain an advantage because it would be too indulgent. Envy could become Jealous, which could restore Willpower when the character takes an opportunity to point out someone else's value as greater than their own. Gluttony could become Indulgent, which could restore Willpower when the character indulges to the point of excess for excess' sake. And Lust could become Lascivious, which could restore Willpower when the character objectifies another character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}